# HTTP Controllers

## Success response

Always set **status**, **description**, and **type** on `@Response` from `@b2b-saas-starter-kit/nest-http`. That decorator also sets `@HttpCode` — do not add a separate `@HttpCode`.

```typescript
@Response({
  status: HttpStatus.CREATED,
  description: 'Tenant created with Owner, Admin, and Member roles',
  type: CreateTenantOutputDto,
})
```

Use `HttpStatus` from `@b2b-saas-starter-kit/contracts` (`OK`, `CREATED`, …), not a magic number.

## Error responses

Every handler must declare the errors it can return with `@ApiErrorResponses` (same package). Document only statuses this route can produce (validation, auth, permission, domain conflict). The type is the shared `ErrorOutputDto` envelope — do not pass a per-route error DTO.

```typescript
@ApiErrorResponses([
  {status: HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, description: 'Request body failed validation'},
  {status: HttpStatus.UNAUTHORIZED, description: 'x-user-id is missing or invalid'},
  {status: HttpStatus.CONFLICT, description: 'Owner user was not found'},
])
```

Do not import `@nestjs/swagger` or `nestjs-zod` in `apps/api`.

## Routes

`@Controller()` takes no path and no version. URI versioning is global (`ApiBuilder.enableVersioning()`, default `'1'`). The **full** resource path lives on the resource `*.routes.ts` object passed to `@ApiRoute`.

```typescript
@Controller()
export class MembersController {
  @ApiRoute(MembersRoutes.list) // path: 'tenants/:tenantId/members'
  list() {}
}
```
